            <ArticleTitle>Coronary air embolism: a case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>897-900</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary air embolism is a complication in the catheterization laboratory that can be associated with high morbidity and even mortality. A case report of air embolism and methods to prevent this complication from occurring are presented along with various management techniques.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
